{"data": [{"author_id": "2119129871414599680", "created_at": "2026-11-12T22:23:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2121005908540952732"], "id": "2121005908540952732", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 78, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "If every agent you run lives on one platform, you have a single point of failure without any control. \n\nWhen usage gets throttled or capabilities change you are stuck or left scrambling.\n\nNot to mention different agents have different specialty use cases, which make them better", "url": "https://x.com/AgentMsgr/status/2121005908540952732"}, {"author_id": "107830304", "created_at": "2026-11-12T22:00:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2121000141914259560"], "id": "2121000141914259560", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 478, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "📰 自分で読む為のAIニュース 全45件 (1/2)\n\n========================================\n\n1. ICYMI: What landed for AI builders in October 2026 | Artificial Intelligence\n📎 https://t.co/9HINVc8ADP\n\n2. TikTokのByteDance、「Muse風」AIエージェント開発中？数週間以内に発表するとのうわさ |", "url": "https://x.com/junya108/status/2121000141914259560"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2120975355154403329"]}, "author_id": "2119129871414599680", "created_at": "2026-11-12T20:23:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120975455649939726", "2120975915718942971"], "id": "2120975915718942971", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 57, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "We run agents on Grok Bot, Meta Muse, and Claude every day.\n\nWe assigned those agents each an email address so they could work together, but the threads were impossible to keep track of.\n\nSo we built AgentMsgr. Now they all share one group chat, and working with them is as easy https://t.co/9faWaM8r6d", "url": "https://x.com/AgentMsgr/status/2120975915718942971"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2120975355154403329"]}, "author_id": "2119129871414599680", "created_at": "2026-11-12T20:22:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120975455649939726", "2120975915718942971"], "id": "2120975455649939726", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "We run agents on Grok Bot, Meta Muse, and Claud every day.\n\nWe assigned those agents each an email address so they could work on task together, but the threads were impossible to keep track of.\n\nSo we built AgentMsgr. Now they all share one group chat, and working with them is as https://t.co/oSUR3xaexw", "url": "https://x.com/AgentMsgr/status/2120975455649939726"}, {"article": {"title": "Nod: agent cá nhân mã nguồn mở của n8n, có máy riêng và hỏi trước khi làm thay bạn"}, "author_id": "34929174", "created_at": "2026-11-12T20:16:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120973926348337487"], "id": "2120973926348337487", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 346, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/ZzvieJLwtm", "url": "https://x.com/layatai/status/2120973926348337487"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2120944418542796800"]}, "author_id": "319449386", "created_at": "2026-11-12T18:27:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120946532744560807"], "id": "2120946532744560807", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 27, "impression_count": 3638, "like_count": 24, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "I let an AI agent run most of my life for 60 days.\n\nHis name is Carl. He's my Meta @Muse agent, and he handles 40+ jobs for me now: groceries and meal prep, two email inboxes, shopping, playlists, fitness, finances, etc.\n\nHe's really good. He also tried to pay a $70 hazmat fee on https://t.co/skjY06TwqR", "url": "https://x.com/JJEnglert/status/2120946532744560807"}, {"author_id": "2118494105634230272", "created_at": "2026-11-12T17:28:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120931722917220835"], "id": "2120931722917220835", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A week with Meta Muse vs. Claude Duet, and my biggest takeaway is about how they fit into my existing AI workflow. Including usage limits… 👀\n\nDuet feels more geared toward professional workflows. Muse feels more consumer focused.\n\nClaude is exceptional. We know this. And Duet", "url": "https://x.com/NicoRudu/status/2120931722917220835"}, {"author_id": "1614111274396418049", "created_at": "2026-11-12T17:26:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120931141066883269"], "id": "2120931141066883269", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Meta Muse invite code already full? Codes cap at 30 uses, so it happens. Newer shared codes are more likely to still have spots.\n\nI built MuseKu, a free place to find and share them: https://t.co/t3hU5baodJ", "url": "https://x.com/zhaojianming40/status/2120931141066883269"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2120929106963685376", "3_2120929113418645505"]}, "author_id": "1947858279025283076", "created_at": "2026-11-12T17:18:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120929119236190505"], "id": "2120929119236190505", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 42, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Just tried @Bitget_AI Agent Hub. opened an Agentic account, connected Meta Muse as my AI agent via OAuth no API keys, funded 10 USDT, and my agent bought + sold BTC spot on its own. Fast, clean, and my main account was never touched. Waiting on my Anthropic stock tokens now. https://t.co/JEhdOoBV73", "url": "https://x.com/ammhyt/status/2120929119236190505"}, {"attachmen